{"title":"Parliamentary Society of Toronto","startsAt":"2026-10-06T17:45:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-06T19:45:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"Ever sat through a meeting and wondered why someone said “I move to table this motion” or “point of order”? Join the Parliamentary Society of Toronto for a hands-on introduction to the rules that govern effective, fair meetings everywhere — from city council to your local condo board.\nWhether you're a community volunteer, a board member, a student, or just curious about how formal meetings actually work, this session is designed to be approachable for complete beginners while still offering value to those with some experience.\n**Society meetings cover:**\n\n1. The basics of Robert's Rules of Order and The Standard Code of Parliamentary Procedure\n1. How motions, amendments, and voting actually work\n1. Common meeting scenarios and how to handle them\n\nThe meeting takes the format of a real business meeting with an agenda , minutes, reports, a business session, etc. During each meeting some aspect of deliberative assemblies is highlighted in an educational essay.","venue":{"name":"Toronto City Hall","address":"Toronto City Hall, Toronto","lat":43.65344,"lng":-79.38409,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"Parliamentary Society of Toronto","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/e/e/0/highres_535687904.jpeg"}